        "message": "LU-20866 o2iblnd: return tunables setup error\n\nkiblnd_tun_defaults() returns 0 when kiblnd_tunables_setup() fails.\nThus, lnet_genl_parse_local_ni() never rejects a NI whose default o2ib\ntunables are invalid (e.g. a bad ib_mtu module parameter). The failure\nis only caught later in kiblnd_startup(), with \"Error -22 starting up\nLNI\" instead of \"default tunables are invalid\".\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: f0a05f7c22 (\"LU-19195 lnet: properly initialize LND tunables\")\nSigned-off-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I49176cde52761f1998b319d12a59402a5a245c44\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69375\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
